>What should I have done?


  Conducts seem to be in Nethack to allow added challenge to expert
players.  You may not be at that level yet, especially if you're asking
for help here.

  I.e.: Don't play conducts you're not ready for.


  Some ideas from a non vegan/vegetarian player:


  - Wizards seem to be the wrong class to play vegan/vegetarian,
especially if you get into trouble you can't handle without prayer.
(A vegan wizard seems like something a player would do just before
moving on from Nethack to a different game entirely.)


  - You should have kept running after fleeing the water elemental.
When you're already in trouble is no time to start fighting another pack
of monsters.

  - As someone else pointed out, Elbereth would have kept the water
elemental from lowering your HP to begin with.

  - Had you done Sokoban yet?  There should be a good chance of food
rations in Soko.  The Voluntary Challenges Spoiler seems to show food
rations are vegan.

  - The Oracle level could have given you spellbooks.  Those might have
given you alternatives.

  - What was your AC?  At that point I'd like for my wizards to have AC
below 0 and dropping as quickly as possible, and forget offensive
spellcasting in combat.   A number of spells can be cast offline and
still help in combat.  When playing a wizard you need to know exactly
what every spell you have does.   More importantly, you need to know the
exact situations those effects will help in.


  - Were you flinging daggers early and often?  It doesn't look like it.
It also looks like you found the problem with playing early wizards as
attack spellcasters:  Poor armor and limited offense.  That's a great
way to die.



  The thing about Nethack is that little actions, or the lack thereof,
can snowball, many turns later, into a situation that's inescapable.
Asking what you should have done at that point usually has one answer:
die.


  It looks like you can't even really play wizards at this point, much
less add a conduct that's particularly difficult for wizards.

  Don't play vegan wizards until you're at least expert at playing a
wizard without conducts.  Ascend four or five wizards in a row first.
NetHack is hard.  Conducts make it harder.


   Summary: Don't Do That Then.  


   Advice: The best way to get out of trouble in NetHack is to avoid
getting into trouble in the first place.



